  partName: Left Rear Cap
  description: The Left Rear Cap is a tiny but essential component located at the
    middle-center-rear of the jet engine, working in conjunction with other caps
    to provide a secure and stable mounting point for the engine's shaft. Its compact
    design and high-strength material, such as Shaft1 2, enable it to withstand the
    high stresses and loads generated by the engine's operation. The Left Rear Cap
    plays a vital role in maintaining the engine's overall balance and stability.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8fad5d10063e3f042ac13d7804d08944, type: 3}
